{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778524195813,"sessionID":"ses_1e7c6c732ffe7065eXF0EcNKOF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9502cdc786d68dbb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"task-coordinator","description":"Coordinate the restructuring of primary hypophysitis and its subtypes in the MONDO ontology.","prompt":"Plan the task to address issue #9859: 'primary hypophysitis synonyms'.\n\nThe issue reports that 'lymphocytic hypophysitis' is currently a synonym of 'primary hypophysitis' (MONDO:0019835), but it should be a subtype.\n\nCurrent state:\n- MONDO:0019835 (primary hypophysitis) has synonyms 'autoimmune hypophysitis' and 'lymphocytic hypophysitis'.\n- There are existing anatomical subtypes of primary hypophysitis:\n    - MONDO:0019838 adenohypophysitis\n    - MONDO:0019839 panhypophysitis\n    - MONDO:0016534 infundibulo-neurohypophysitis\n\nKey information from the issue:\n- Primary hypophysitis is a parent term for lymphocytic hypophysitis.\n- Lymphocytic hypophysitis is the most common histopathological subtype of primary hypophysitis.\n- Primary hypophysitis can be divided into histopathologic (lymphocytic, granulomatous, xanthomatous, IgG4-related, necrotizing) and anatomical types.\n- Anatomical classification (LAH, LINH, LPH) applies specifically to lymphocytic hypophysitis.\n\nGoals:\n1. Research the relationship between 'primary hypophysitis', 'autoimmune hypophysitis', and 'lymphocytic hypophysitis'.\n2. Remove 'lymphocytic hypophysitis' as a synonym of MONDO:0019835.\n3. Create a new term for 'lymphocytic hypophysitis' (MONDO:777xxxx) and make it a subclass of MONDO:0019835.\n4. Determine if 'autoimmune hypophysitis' should remain a synonym of 'primary hypophysitis' or be moved.\n5. Investigate if existing anatomical subtypes (MONDO:0019838, MONDO:0019839, MONDO:0016534) should be moved to be subclasses of the new 'lymphocytic hypophysitis' term, given the claim that anatomical subclassification applies specifically to it.\n6. Ensure proper citations and metadata are used.\n\nPlease provide a detailed sequence of agents and validation steps.","subagent_type":"general"},"output":"task_id: ses_1e7b84095ffeXTxUnOhrf4Ihp8 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nTo address issue #9859, I will follow this sequence of agents and validation steps:\n\n### 1. Research & Design Phase\n- **`deep-research-specialist`**: Investigate the relationship between primary, autoimmune, and lymphocytic hypophysitis. Verify if anatomical subtypes (MONDO:0019838, 0019839, 0016534) are specifically subtypes of lymphocytic hypophysitis.\n- **`design-pattern-advisor`**: Identify the appropriate design pattern for creating the new 'lymphocytic hypophysitis' term.\n\n### 2. Execution Phase\n- **Term Modification**:\n    - Use `obo-checkout.pl` to extract MONDO:0019835 and relevant anatomical subtypes.\n    - Remove \"lymphocytic hypophysitis\" as a synonym of **MONDO:0019835**.\n    - Create a new term for **lymphocytic hypophysitis** (MONDO:777xxxx) as a subclass of MONDO:0019835.\n    - Adjust the hierarchy of anatomical subtypes if research confirms they belong under lymphocytic hypophysitis.\n    - Resolve the status of \"autoimmune hypophysitis\" based on research.\n\n### 3. Validation & Quality Control\n- **`identifier-validator`**: Verify all newly added PMIDs and external IDs.\n- **`metadata-checker`**: Ensure the new term has a valid definition, source attribution, and required metadata.\n- **`odk`**: Perform syntax validation using `robot convert`.\n- **`ontology-reasoner`**: Check for logical inconsistencies or unsatisfiable classes resulting from the hierarchy change.\n\n### 4. Finalization\n- **Integration**: Use `obo-checkin.pl` to commit changes to `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`.\n- **Normalization**: Run `sh run.sh make NORM && mv NORM mondo-edit.obo` to normalize the serialization.\n</task_result>","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_1e7b84095ffeXTxUnOhrf4Ihp8","model":{"modelID":"google/gemma-4-31B-it","providerID":"togetherai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Coordinate the restructuring of primary hypophysitis and its subtypes in the MONDO ontology.","time":{"start":1778523815803,"end":1778524195809}},"id":"prt_e184649e9001r41kHzi7QpEMka","sessionID":"ses_1e7c6c732ffe7065eXF0EcNKOF","messageID":"msg_e18443c92001zeV3qoQ7Ux0yKr"}}
